<title>UK: Lloyd's fund NLC acquires 20 pct stake in Crowe.</title>
<headline>Lloyd's fund NLC acquires 20 pct stake in Crowe.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>New London Capital, the Lloyd's of London investment company, said on Thursday it was to buy a 20 percent stake in Crowe Insurance as part of a deal under which the two form a dedicated Lloyd's capital vehicle.</p>
<p>NLC will invest 7.3 million stg and hold 55 percent of the vehicle, which will have initial assets of 9.3 million stg.</p>
<p>The venture will support the six Lloyd's insurance syndicates managed by Crowe and will underwrite capacity of 38 million stg in the 1997 year. Capacity is the amount the insurance market can underwrite in terms of premium income.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7721</p>
</text>
